What you need is probably something in Window_Message, not Game_Message… which makes things slightly tricky, because there's no simple way to get the Window_Message.
Maybe this will work?
JavaScript:
let win = Scene_Manager._scene._windowLayer.children.find(win => win instanceof Window_Message);
if(win) win.pause = false;
I haven't tested it though. Also, even if it works, you'll probably need additional logic to deal with choice windows, pick item, or input number.

maybe try this in scriptcall (I put it from my altMessageWindow
Code:
if ($gameMessage.isBusy()) {
     $gameMessage.clear();
     if (SceneManager._scene._messageWindow) {
          SceneManager._scene._messageWindow.close();
      }
or maybe simplified:
Code:
if ($gameMessage.isBusy()) {
     $gameMessage.clear();
     SceneManager._scene?._messageWindow.close()
but it check if the game message is busy first, than close it when possible.
only my altMessageWindow check if the player is walking as well to close it.

